WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.270
If you're a pet parent like me,

2
00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.791
and a lot of you guys are!

3
00:00:03.791 --> 00:00:06.370
(audience cheering)
That's right!

4
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.580
Makes me so happy there's so many of us here in this room.

5
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.610
And for those who are watching,

6
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.950
you know what a challenge it can be

7
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.280
to keep your furry friends fresh and clean, no joke.

8
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.600 line:15%
And that's why I was so excited to team up with PetSmart

9
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.170 line:15%
and introduce my dogs, Douglas and Lucy,

10
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.810
to their top groomers.

11
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.470
Take a look.

12
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.310
Hi, guys.
[Ashley And Kristie] Hi.

13
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.040
How are you?
Good, how are you?

14
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.500
So nice to meet you guys.

15
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.020
We are so excited to meet Lucy and Douglas today.

16
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.450 line:15%
This is Lucy, and that's Douglas.

17
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.710 line:15%
And they're very much in love.

18
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.710
They've been together almost nine years now.

19
00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.000
Aw.
Aw.

20
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.170
Best friends too, you can tell.

21
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.200
Yeah, they're very different dogs.

22
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.940
They have very different coats.

23
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.810
Lucy's hair, it's so grody from the New York City streets.

24
00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:00.400
What is your advice on how often

25
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.620 line:15%
I should groom Lucy?

26
00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.010 line:15%
I would recommend probably every four to six weeks

27
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.760 line:15%
for more of a FURminator treatment.

28
00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.160 line:15%
'Cause you wanna get that undercoat out,

29
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.000 line:15%
'cause she looks like she sheds a lot.

30
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.740 line:15%
But it's more than just the FURminator,

31
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.000 line:15%
it's really the whole process.

32
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.790 line:15%
The brush, specialized shampoo, conditioner and a blowout.

33
00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.160
So really get that undercoat out

34
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.880
'cause that's also what's gonna attract a lot of that dirt.

35
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.740
So I brought the FURminator with me.

36
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.600
And so do you want me to show you how to use it?

37
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.300
I mean, I have four cats, two dogs,

38
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.340
six chickens, a bearded dragon.

39
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.993
Oh, and a fish named Blueberry.

40
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.760
My house is kind of covered in animal hair.

41
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.140
So is this a solution?

42
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.060
Yes, definitely, because I'm sure

43
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.770
you probably can't wear black pants a lot.

44
00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.970
Oh, I mean, if I was a human lint roller,

45
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.123
that would help.

46
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.500 line:15%
What you do is you just go along the growth

47
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.540 line:15%
and not a lot of pressure.

48
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.481 line:15%
See all that hair?
But see all

49
00:01:52.481 --> 00:01:53.981 line:15%
this stuff coming out?

50
00:01:53.981 --> 00:01:55.320 line:15%
(Kristie laughing)

51
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.077 line:15%
That's with three strokes.

52
00:01:57.077 --> 00:01:58.780 line:15%
And in the salon, like Ashley said,

53
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.140 line:15%
they'll get the full treatment.

54
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.659 line:15%
So it's the shampoo, the conditioner,

55
00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:04.810 line:15%
drying, as well as the brushing.

56
00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.810
You could go to the salon.

57
00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.020
What does it take to become a groomer at a PetSmart?

58
00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.750
Oh gosh, it's such a commitment.

59
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.890
Most all of our stylists start out as a bather

60
00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.900
and they work their way up through our training program,

61
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.730 line:15%
over 800 hours of classroom time with hands-on training

62
00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:24.840 line:15%
to learn all different types of dogs, breed knowledge.

63
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.620
And you have to be so passionate

64
00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.410
about animals to do what we do.

65
00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.450
because you take all kinds.

66
00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.430
And we don't just groom dogs in our salons,

67
00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.440
we also groom cats and felines.

68
00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.400
What about bearded dragons?

69
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.040 line:15%
Because Jeremy, if you think I've got dry legs,

70
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.370 line:15%
you should meet Jeremy.

71
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.530 line:15%
We don't do bearded dragon grooming yet,

72
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.730 line:15%
but maybe in the future.

73
00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.583 line:15%
You never know.
I'm telling you.

74
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:51.370 line:15%
I mean, I love that it takes that long

75
00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:53.940
to train to become a groomer

76
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.940
so that the customer and the owner feel so safe.

77
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.990
I mean, we've been with PetSmart a long time.

78
00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.070
Like this is my 20th year with the company.

79
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.540
And Kristie has been with us.

80
00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.700
14 years now.

81
00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.330 line:15%
And she's also our top 10 member for Groom Team USA.

82
00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.163 line:15%
I am.

83
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.560 line:15%
Okay, but then what do you recommend for Douglas?

84
00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.900
I would recommend our HEMPZ Package,

85
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:21.320
which is a really good shampoo, conditioning treatment,

86
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.380
you wanna add moisture back into that coat.

87
00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:24.890
I'd also do nail grinding,

88
00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.520
which helps keep the nails really nice,

89
00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.210
and short, and smooth so that if he jumps up,

90
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.790
won't scratch the kids

91
00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.610
or keeps them nice and short

92
00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.950
around the house on hardwood floors.

93
00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.510 line:15%
This is a Dremel, but it has a special head on it for dogs.

94
00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.770 line:15%
So it does make the nail warm or hot,

95
00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.960 line:15%
it's just the vibration that feels a little funny.

96
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.920 line:15%
Well, I would like some of that.

97
00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.700
Feels really nice.

98
00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.930
So now that we've brushed them out and done some stuff,

99
00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.460
we have our summer collection of bandanas here.

100
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.510
Would you like to pick out something for each of them?

101
00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:55.900
It's gonna be hard to choose because I'm so into them.

102
00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.733
But yeah.

103
00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.080
I think I'm gonna go for these two.

104
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.970
No shocker here, I'm gonna go with the flowers.

105
00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.160
It's my fave.
And then, I'm definitely

106
00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.450
going with the popsicle motif,

107
00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.669
because these are just sparking a lot of joy.

108
00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:15.252
(upbeat music)

109
00:04:28.345 --> 00:04:30.674
I mean, look at them!

110
00:04:30.674 --> 00:04:32.160
Oh, that whole segment I was like,

111
00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.340
"Look at that dog, look at that dog."

112
00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.160
I just wanna give a huge thank you

113
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.190
to Ashley and Kristie from PetSmart

114
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.840
for showing me all the amazing services they offer.

115
00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.690
And if you wanna pamper your furry friends,

116
00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:46.880 line:15%
head over to PetSmart.com to book a grooming

117
00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.950 line:15%
or just a walk-in for a standalone service.

118
00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.640
And we want our studio audience to get in on all the fun,

119
00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.020
so you're all going home

120
00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:58.081
with a $100 gift card from PetSmart!

121
00:04:58.081 --> 00:04:59.596
(audience cheering)

122
00:04:59.596 --> 00:05:02.179 line:15%
(upbeat music)

